Hot-spot shift experiment: client-side load-shift hardcode.

Reproduces benchmark/hotspot_shift.pdf, where the hot region moves from
validator 0 to validator 1 mid-run and the LB algorithm has to re-converge.

Origin: commits 5468daa ("script and results", April) and the hotspot block
fixes from 3b4a41f, both on branch zp/hotspot-shift-v2, replayed onto
zp/multi-client-lb. consensus/src/lib.rs is already byte-identical between the
two branches, and this branch additionally carries cffe261 (2f+1 client
confirmations to reroute), so nothing outside the client needs patching.

Kept out of the branch because cloudlab_bench.py hardcodes the shift as
"region 0 <-> region 1 at 2.5*WARMUP seconds", which is specific to this figure.

Apply/run/unapply via: benchmark/exp/run_hotspot_shift.sh

